Performance Evaluation of Ultra-Wideband Vivaldi Antenna Arrays with Emphasis on Grating Lobes, and Mutual Coupling 
Abstract— Ultra-wideband (UWB) antennas find extensive use in various wireless communication and radar systems. 
They offer wide bandwidth and constant radiation characteristics.
 In this paper, the performance evaluation of Vivaldi antenna arrays at 6 GHz is carried out using MATLAB Antenna Toolbox.
 Various antenna parameters, including VSWR, radiation pattern, input impedance, mutual coupling, and grating lobes, have been investigated for various antenna array sizes and interelement spacings.
 It has been found that when the spacing is 0.8λ, grating lobes do not occur, and VSWR is below 2. 
However, if the spacing is increased, grating lobes occur. 
It has also been found that by increasing the number of antenna elements, the antenna gain and directivity can be increased, but at the same time, mutual coupling is increased. 
. It has been found that Vivaldi antenna arrays offer optimal performance.
